---
import Navigation from "../../components/navigation.astro";
import { posts } from "../../data/posts.js";

const post = posts.find((post) => post.slug === "post_one");

if (!post) {
  throw new Error("Blog post not found.");
}

const { title, date, tags } = post;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>{title} | Ivy Duncan</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Ivy Duncan talks about finally getting around to making an author website."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navigation />

    <main>
      <article class="blog-post">
        <div class="container narrow">
          <a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to Blog</a>

          <header class="post-header">
  <p class="eyebrow">From the Blog</p>

  <h1>{title}</h1>

  <p class="post-date">{date}</p>

  <div class="post-tags">
    {
      tags.map((tag) => (
        <a
          href={`/blog/tag/${tag.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}`}
          class="post-tag"
        >
          {tag}
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</header>

          <div class="post-content">
            <p>
              It’s all very exciting. I’ve been writing for over ten years
              now (wow, I feel old), and I’ve been a published author for a
              few years, but I’m just now finally getting around to making
              a website.
            </p>

            <p>
              I love writing, and it’s definitely my passion, but there’s a
              lot more that goes into it besides coming up with stories and
              putting them on paper, and I’m honestly not all that great at
              all the other stuff. My social media barely gets updated, and
              I just recently got <em>If it’s Meant to Be</em> on Barnes and
              Noble even though it’s been out for months.
            </p>

            <p>
              Full time job + naturally lazy + trying to be a “proper”
              author = things falling through the cracks.
            </p>

            <p>
              But an author website is no longer one of those things!
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-footer">
            <a href="/blog" class="button button-secondary">
              Back to Blog
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="container">
        <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ivy Duncan. All rights reserved.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    background: #faf9f6;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #faf9f6;
    color: #2f2924;
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
  }

  .container {
    width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .blog-post {
    padding: 5rem 0 6rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: #765f48;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .post-header {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .post-date {
    margin: 0;
    color: #765f48;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .post-tags {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 1.25rem;
}

.post-tag {
  color: #765f48;
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  text-decoration: none;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.post-tag:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
}

  .post-content {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }

  .post-content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(118 95 72 / 20%);
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid #765f48;
    transition:
      background-color 0.2s ease,
      color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .button-secondary {
    color: #765f48;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .button-secondary:hover {
    color: #fff;
    background: #765f48;
  }

  .site-footer {
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(118 95 72 / 15%);
    color: #765f48;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .site-footer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .container {
      width: min(100% - 2rem, 1100px);
    }

    .blog-post {
      padding: 3.5rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .back-link {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .post-header {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .post-content {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }
  }
</style>